parts.text:
The user clarified: "Все кнопки, которые отвечают за заказ. Чтобы не было так, что человек нажал заказать на карточке, а потом при переходе выбрал подписку. А в запили оставался Разовый заказ."

So: all order-related buttons should be synchronized. If a user clicks "заказать" on a card (sets Разовый заказ + comment), and then in the form switches to "Подписка", the comment should update accordingly (not keep "Разовый заказ: ..."). I.e., the radio selection and the comment must stay consistent.

So the logic:
- Clicking "заказать →" on a card: selects radio "Разовый заказ" and sets comment to "Разовый заказ: <товар>".
- If the user then changes the radio to "Подписка" (or "Вопрос"), the comment should update to match the new interest. And if they switch back to "Разовый заказ", the comment should restore the product text (or clear appropriately).

Essentially: switching interest radio should also update the comment text so it never contradicts.

Let me design the behavior:
- Maintain a stored product string (last clicked product), say `lastProduct`.
- On radio change: 
  - if value == 'one-time': comment = lastProduct ? 'Разовый заказ: ' + lastProduct : '' (or leave)
  - if value == 'subscription': comment = 'Подписка: 2 пачки в месяц' (or clear)
  - if value == 'question': comment = '' (clear)
- On "заказать" click: set radio to one-time, set lastProduct, set comment.

But should we overwrite user's manually typed comment? That could be annoying. Better: only manage the comment if it hasn't been manually edited, OR always prepend/replace a managed line. Simplest consistent approach: keep a "managed" comment prefix. Hmm.

The user's concern: comment says "Разовый заказ: X" while radio says "Подписка" → mismatch. So when radio changes, update the comment.

A clean approach: The comment reflects the interest. Let me:
- Track `orderText` (product) separately.
- Render comment = buildComment(interest, orderText):
  - subscription → "Подписка: 2 пачки в месяц" + (orderText? ...). Hmm, if they picked a product then chose subscription, maybe comment could include product too? Maybe commentary should reflect both. But simplest: base text per interest.

Let me keep it simple and predictable:
- subscription → "Подписка — 2 пачки в месяц"
- one-time → orderText ? ("Разовый заказ: " + orderText) : "Разовый заказ"
- question → "" (empty, user types)

And when user clicks "заказать" on a card, it sets interest=one-time and orderText=product → comment = "Разовый заказ: <product>".

When user manually edits the comment, we should stop auto-overwriting? The user's concern is about the mismatch from button flows. If a user types their own comment and then switches interest, overwriting their typing is bad. Solution: only auto-update the comment if the current comment is one we generated (i.e., not manually edited). Track a flag `managed = true` set when we write the comment; if the user types in the textarea → managed = false; then radio changes won't overwrite.

But then the mismatch could happen if user typed manually. However the mismatch concern is specifically about the button flow. If they type their own, it's their text — fine.

Hmm, but user might type after picking a product, then switch — edge. Let's implement: radio change updates comment only if comment is currently "managed" (auto). Once user edits manually, we stop. That's the least surprising.

Also: should the radio change happen even when clicking "оформить подписку" button (in subcard)? Yes! The subcard button "Оформить подписку" currently is an anchor `href="#contact"` and doesn't set the radio. The user says "Все кнопки, которые отвечают за заказ" — all order buttons. So:
- "Оставить заявку" (hero) — generic, leave as is (just scroll).
- "Оформить подписку" (subcard) — should set radio to subscription + set comment "Подписка...".
- "заказать →" on cards — set one-time + product.
- "Отправить заявку" (submit) — the actual order button.

So I need to add data-order-like handling for the subscription button.

Let me implement:
- data attributes: `data-interest="one-time" data-order="Эфиопия..."` on card buttons; `data-interest="subscription"` on subcard button.
- A generic handler for any element with `data-interest`.

Let me rewrite the script:

```js
var commentEl = document.getElementById('d-comment');
var autoComment = true; // whether comment is managed by us
var lastProduct = '';

function setInterest(value){ 
  var r = document.querySelector('input[name="interest"][value="'+value+'"]');
  if (r) r.checked = true;
}
function buildComment(value){
  if (value === 'subscription') return 'Подписка — 2 пачки в месяц';
  if (value === 'one-time') return lastProduct ? ('Разовый заказ: ' + lastProduct) : 'Разовый заказ';
  return '';
}
function applyInterest(value){
  setInterest(value);
  if (autoComment && commentEl){ commentEl.value = buildComment(value); }
}

document.querySelectorAll('[data-interest]').forEach(function(el){
  el.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    var value = el.getAttribute('data-interest');
    if (value === 'one-time'){ lastProduct = el.getAttribute('data-order') || lastProduct; }
    applyInterest(value);
    var t = document.getElementById('contact');
    if (t) t.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'});
  });
});

document.querySelectorAll('input[name="interest"]').forEach(function(r){
  r.addEventListener('change', function(){
    if (autoComment && commentEl) commentEl.value = buildComment(r.value);
  });
});

if (commentEl){ commentEl.addEventListener('input', function(){ autoComment = false; }); }
```

This satisfies: click "заказать" → one-time + comment "Разовый заказ: X". Then in form switch to Подписка → comment becomes "Подписка — 2 пачки в месяц" (no stale "Разовый заказ"). Switch back to Разовый заказ → "Разовый заказ: X" restored (lastProduct remembered). Good.

Also "Оформить подписку" → sets subscription + comment.

Note: the radio labels use `:has(input:checked)` for styling — works.

Now update the HTML: 
- subcard button: `<a class="btn2" href="#contact" data-interest="subscription">Оформить подписку</a>`
- card buttons: `<span class="add" data-interest="one-time" data-order="...">заказать →</span>`
- hero button: keep href="#contact".

Let me edit d.html: replace the script and the button attributes.

Let me do the edits.

Also, should I update the lab? The lab is a tool; the final D is what matters. Let me also keep the lab? The user is reviewing D now. I'll leave lab.

But wait — the user's original ask "Переключение по кнопкам, чтобы тоже меняло текст комментария" was about D's form. Now clarified. Let me implement in D.

Then commit #9, and propose next: build the real app in Next.

Let me make the edits.

First, edit the subcard button.

Current: `<a class="btn2" href="#contact">Оформить подписку</a>`
→ `<a class="btn2" href="#contact" data-interest="subscription">Оформить подписку</a>`

Card buttons: `<span class="add" data-order="Эфиопия Иргачеффе, 250 г">заказать →</span>` → add data-interest="one-time". There are 4. Use replaceAll on `class="add" data-order=` → `class="add" data-interest="one-time" data-order=`. 

Actually replaceAll `data-order=` → `data-interest="one-time" data-order=` would hit 4 occurrences. Good.

Then replace the script block.

Let me do it.

